/**
 * Dev environment seed — fake accounts + fixtures for every major surface.
 *
 *   npx tsx scripts/seed-dev.ts            # create / refresh everything
 *   npx tsx scripts/seed-dev.ts --reset    # delete seeded rows, then re-create
 *   npx tsx scripts/seed-dev.ts --plan     # print what would be seeded, no writes
 *   npx tsx scripts/seed-dev.ts --no-bulk  # personas + scenarios only, skip the volume layer
 *
 * Safety: refuses to run unless `.env.local` points at the DEV Supabase project
 * (`rbtdomefinsrclgubpuf`). Both the URL and the service-role JWT are checked.
 *
 * Idempotent: every row id is a UUID v5 of a stable key under SEED_NS, so a
 * re-run upserts in place. Accounts are created through `auth.admin.createUser`
 * so the `handle_new_user` trigger fires and every persona can really sign in.
 * Dates are relative to the run, so "upcoming" stays upcoming.
 *
 * Credentials: fake personas share `DEV_SEED_PASSWORD`; the admin account
 * (Britton) uses `DEV_SEED_ADMIN_PASSWORD`. Both are read from `.env.local` and
 * generated + appended there on first run. The full list lives in the
 * "Dev Seed and Test Accounts" doc.
 */

